WEBVTT

00:02.419 --> 00:03.351
Hi.

00:03.353 --> 00:05.820
This is Jeff;
Jeff Strongman.

00:06.889 --> 00:08.523
So what happened
between you and your girl?

00:08.525 --> 00:11.426
She wanted to get married and
I'm just not sure I'm ready.

00:11.428 --> 00:13.061
It's the same reason
I lost Lyndsey.

00:13.063 --> 00:14.662
It's like we were
dating the same woman.

00:14.664 --> 00:17.499
I am gonna ask Lyndsey
to marry me.

00:18.134 --> 00:19.534
Lyndsey MacElroy...

00:19.536 --> 00:20.769
will you marry me?

00:20.771 --> 00:22.704
Yes! I will marry you!

00:22.706 --> 00:24.973
Everything you need to know
is right in here.

00:24.975 --> 00:28.410
Somebody gave me
a billion dollar idea--

00:28.412 --> 00:29.878
thought controlled computing.

00:29.880 --> 00:31.212
We have so much work to do

00:31.214 --> 00:33.181
and all I can think about
is you and me-- wow...

00:33.183 --> 00:34.749
Gotta stop thinking about sex.

00:34.751 --> 00:36.384
This is Walden Schmidt
saying--

00:36.386 --> 00:38.153
FEMALE COMPUTER VOICE:
Pudding.

00:38.155 --> 00:40.098
I think the computer
just read his thoughts!

00:40.123 --> 00:40.856
It worked.

00:40.857 --> 00:42.624
(screams happily)
(laughs) Yes!

00:42.626 --> 00:44.626
FEMALE COMPUTER VOICE:
Someone's not wearing a bra.

00:44.628 --> 00:46.895
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

00:47.437 --> 00:48.636
This is great!

00:48.638 --> 00:50.004
My best friend, my fiancée

00:50.006 --> 00:51.606
and a great bottle
of French wine.

00:51.608 --> 00:54.175
Uh, uh, technically
it's French Canadian.

00:54.177 --> 00:56.143
Uh, it's called
"Two-buck Canuck,"

00:56.145 --> 00:59.080
and, uh, it's not wine,
it's wine-ish.

00:59.082 --> 01:00.715
Um, but it still gets
the panties on the floor,

01:00.717 --> 01:02.116
if you know
what I'm talking about.

01:02.118 --> 01:03.250
(laughter)

01:03.252 --> 01:05.052
Maybe you should have
another glass, Lyndsey.

01:05.054 --> 01:06.120
I'm good.

01:06.122 --> 01:07.788
Hey, uh, how about you, Larry?

01:07.790 --> 01:10.324
No, I'm not wearing panties.

01:10.326 --> 01:14.362
All righty, so, uh,
guess we're done with this.

01:14.364 --> 01:15.763
So...

01:15.765 --> 01:17.632
how long of an engagement
are you guys planning?

01:17.634 --> 01:19.033
Uh, two years? Five years?

01:19.035 --> 01:20.968
I mean, you know, there's
no rush to start a family.

01:20.970 --> 01:22.603
I mean, after all, uh,

01:22.605 --> 01:25.106
Lyndsey's well beyond
her child-bearing age.

01:26.274 --> 01:28.342
Well, we have talked about
adopting a baby from China.

01:28.344 --> 01:29.413
Oh!

01:29.438 --> 01:30.679
Course, then we'd
have to teach it English,

01:30.680 --> 01:32.680
which seems like a lot of work.

01:32.682 --> 01:35.249
Would you mind
getting desert, sweetie?

01:35.251 --> 01:37.451
Sure.
Sure.

01:38.687 --> 01:39.687
Um, kidding.

01:39.689 --> 01:41.989
Uh, this one's on you, sweetie.

01:41.991 --> 01:43.224
(Alan &amp; Larry laughing)

01:43.226 --> 01:44.959
All right, but no funny business
while I'm gone.

01:44.961 --> 01:45.960
I'll know, Jeff.

01:45.962 --> 01:47.361
(laughs)
You haven't so far.

01:47.363 --> 01:49.030
I've been banging this one
for months.

01:50.198 --> 01:52.133
(Alan &amp; Larry guffawing)

01:52.135 --> 01:53.300
LYNDSEY: Oh...!
I love this guy!

01:53.302 --> 01:55.002
She does too!
(laughing)

01:55.004 --> 01:56.337
(laughing)

01:57.439 --> 01:58.773
Isn't this fun?

01:58.775 --> 02:00.641
(laughing):
Yeah. It's great.

02:00.643 --> 02:02.610
Why the hell are you here?

02:02.612 --> 02:03.744
Larry asked me to dinner.

02:03.746 --> 02:05.312
What was I supposed to say?

02:05.314 --> 02:07.014
That you couldn't come.
That you had to work.

02:07.016 --> 02:08.449
That you're not really
Jeff Strongman

02:08.451 --> 02:10.351
and your entire friendship
is a lie.

02:10.353 --> 02:12.386
That I had to work--
that's a good one.

02:12.388 --> 02:14.388
(sighs)

02:14.390 --> 02:17.892
Alan, this wedding
is very important to me.

02:17.894 --> 02:19.927
If you still have
any feelings for me at all,

02:19.929 --> 02:21.729
you will let me have this day.

02:21.731 --> 02:22.997
Fine.

02:23.832 --> 02:24.932
I shan't go.

02:24.934 --> 02:26.367
(sighs)

02:26.369 --> 02:27.802
But good luck getting
the Chicken Dance

02:27.804 --> 02:29.336
started without me.

02:31.673 --> 02:33.541
Hey, Jeff, you want
a piece of Lyndsey's pie?

02:33.543 --> 02:35.910
There's no way
I can eat it all myself.

02:35.912 --> 02:37.344
I don't know.

02:37.346 --> 02:38.979
Last time I had some,
there was a hair in it.

02:38.981 --> 02:42.783
Jeff was actually just saying
that he's got to get going.

02:42.785 --> 02:44.351
Mm.
Really? Oh.

02:44.353 --> 02:45.753
Well, then I'll
make this quick.

02:45.755 --> 02:48.422
I know we haven't known
each other for a long time,

02:48.424 --> 02:50.257
but I feel like
we share a lot.

02:50.259 --> 02:52.126
M-More than you know.

02:52.128 --> 02:54.261
So I was wondering
if you'd do me the honor

02:54.263 --> 02:55.396
of being my best man?

02:55.398 --> 02:56.997
What?!
What?!

02:56.999 --> 02:58.199
What do you say?

02:58.201 --> 03:00.000
I... say...

03:00.869 --> 03:01.936
...you've made me
the happiest

03:01.938 --> 03:03.003
person in the world-- yes!

03:03.005 --> 03:05.473
(laughing)

03:05.475 --> 03:08.175
You sure? Don't you want to
take a moment to think about it?

03:08.177 --> 03:09.376
What is there
to think about?

03:09.378 --> 03:10.544
You know, you could
change my name from

03:10.546 --> 03:12.580
"Jeff Strongman",
to "Jeff Best Man."

03:12.582 --> 03:13.948
(both laughing)

03:13.950 --> 03:15.516
That's the kind of stuff
I want in your toast!

03:15.518 --> 03:17.318
And this is the
kind of stuff

03:17.320 --> 03:18.853
you're gonna get
on the dance floor:

03:18.855 --> 03:22.556
(singing "Chicken Dance" melody)

03:22.558 --> 03:23.657
(both grunting in rhythm)

03:23.659 --> 03:25.159
(both laughing)

03:25.161 --> 03:27.728
♪ Men, men, men, men, manly men,
men, men ♪

03:27.730 --> 03:28.397
♪ Ah.
♪ Men.♪

03:28.398 --> 03:32.398
&lt;font color="#00FF00">♪ Two and a Half Men 11x16 ♪&lt;/font>
&lt;font color="#00FFFF">How to Get Rid of Alan Harper&lt;/font>
Original Air Date on March 6, 2014

03:32.399 --> 03:37.399
== sync, corrected by &lt;font color=#00FF00>elderman&lt;/font> ==
&lt;font color=#00FFFF>@elder_man&lt;/font>

03:37.400 --> 03:38.734
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

03:40.612 --> 03:41.813
Oh. Oh. Wait.

03:45.284 --> 03:46.684
FEMALE COMPUTER VOICE:
Hey, good lookin'.

03:46.686 --> 03:48.052
Whatcha got cookin'?

03:49.755 --> 03:50.688
Pot brownies.

03:50.690 --> 03:51.956
What the hell is that?

03:51.958 --> 03:53.758
FEMALE COMPUTER VOICE:
It's a new project

03:53.760 --> 03:54.692
I'm working on.

03:54.694 --> 03:56.494
It enables a computer

03:56.496 --> 03:58.029
to read my mind

03:58.031 --> 04:00.031
and then talk to you.

04:00.033 --> 04:01.899
Why can't you just talk to me?

04:01.901 --> 04:05.136
FEMALE COMPUTER VOICE:
Because, I...

04:05.138 --> 04:07.872
and this... shut up.

04:09.274 --> 04:10.575
Come on, try it.
I think it's big enough.

04:10.577 --> 04:11.542
I think it'll fit.

04:11.544 --> 04:13.578
The last time someone said that,

04:13.580 --> 04:16.347
I ended up pregnant
with my first daughter.

04:17.850 --> 04:20.151
Hey... I got good news.

04:20.153 --> 04:23.487
I'm paid to pick up your crap,
not listen to it.

04:24.423 --> 04:27.525
Guess who Larry asked
to be his best man?

04:27.527 --> 04:30.194
One of his friends
who's actually real?

04:30.196 --> 04:33.531
Jeff Strongman is like butter
on movie theater popcorn.

04:33.533 --> 04:36.434
He may not be real,
but he's delicious  nonetheless.

04:36.436 --> 04:38.402
Okay, so, let me
get this straight:

04:38.404 --> 04:40.605
your alter ego,
Mm-hmm.

04:40.607 --> 04:42.073
is going to be the best man

04:42.075 --> 04:43.674
at the wedding of your lover...

04:43.676 --> 04:45.109
and another guy?

04:45.111 --> 04:47.111
When you put it like that,
it sounds like

04:47.113 --> 04:48.346
a soap opera on Telemundo.

04:48.348 --> 04:49.647
(doorbell rings)

04:49.649 --> 04:50.982
(Spanish accent):
Señor Strongman, why do you

04:50.984 --> 04:53.351
make love to
the woman of the man you love?

04:54.786 --> 04:56.621
Lyndsey?
Are you insane?

04:56.623 --> 04:59.824
&lt;i>Oh, si, Señor Strongman&lt;/i>
&lt;i>es muy loco.&lt;/i>

05:01.360 --> 05:04.061
How could you say "yes",
to being Larry's best man?

05:04.063 --> 05:05.463
I don't know. I got excited.

05:05.465 --> 05:07.932
And you and I both know
when I get excited, I tend to...

05:07.934 --> 05:09.367
react prematurely.

05:09.369 --> 05:11.769
Why would you even want to go?

05:11.771 --> 05:13.170
Are you kidding me?!

05:13.172 --> 05:14.872
I mean, just 'cause
you're mad at me right now

05:14.874 --> 05:16.841
doesn't mean I'm going to miss
the wedding of someone I love.

05:16.843 --> 05:19.410
Aw... that's very sweet.

05:19.412 --> 05:20.811
I was talking about Larry.

05:20.813 --> 05:21.812
Oh!
Ow!

05:21.814 --> 05:23.247
&lt;i>Ah! Dios mío!&lt;/i>

05:25.217 --> 05:27.985
Alan, I don't care
how you do it,

05:27.987 --> 05:29.787
fake Jeff Strongman's death--

05:29.789 --> 05:31.255
actually die.

05:31.257 --> 05:32.924
You will not be at my wedding.

05:35.127 --> 05:36.994
(door slams shut)

05:36.996 --> 05:39.230
(scoffs, laughs)

05:39.232 --> 05:44.068
She will be back here in three
seconds looking for make-up sex.

05:45.103 --> 05:47.271
One...

05:47.273 --> 05:48.572
Two...

05:52.411 --> 05:54.178
FEMALE COMPUTER VOICE:
Three.

05:55.447 --> 05:57.381
Three.

05:59.785 --> 06:01.185
You're an idiot.

06:03.655 --> 06:04.956
I'm, um, I'm sorry.

06:04.958 --> 06:06.123
That was wrong.

06:06.125 --> 06:08.225
&lt;i>Tú eres una idiota.&lt;/i>

06:08.227 --> 06:10.628
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

06:11.930 --> 06:14.165
All right, Bill Gates...

06:14.167 --> 06:16.300
Steve Wozniak...

06:16.302 --> 06:17.435
and Mark Zuckerberg.

06:17.437 --> 06:18.903
Ooh, that's a tough one.
Yeah.

06:18.905 --> 06:21.072
I'd definitely kill
Mark Zuckerberg...

06:22.374 --> 06:24.809
...bang Bill Gates,
marry Steve Wozniak.

06:25.677 --> 06:27.378
What?! That's crazy.

06:27.380 --> 06:30.281
I mean, yes,
you have to kill Zuckerberg.

06:30.283 --> 06:31.615
But you gotta marry Bill.

06:31.617 --> 06:32.750
I mean, I've seen it before,

06:32.752 --> 06:34.318
he is gonna
take those glasses off

06:34.320 --> 06:36.387
and shake is hair loose
and you're gonna be like,

06:36.389 --> 06:38.823
"Where did this guy come from?"

06:38.825 --> 06:41.158
I hear you, but I'm still
marrying Woz.

06:41.160 --> 06:42.626
I'm a boob man.

06:43.628 --> 06:45.730
Are you guys playing
"Bang, Marry, Kill" again?

06:45.732 --> 06:48.132
'Cause if you are,
I've got one for you:

06:48.134 --> 06:52.003
Angelina Jolie,
Mila Kunis and me.

06:52.005 --> 06:53.237
I would kill you

06:53.239 --> 06:55.573
by banging you to death
on our honeymoon.

06:55.575 --> 06:57.108
Aw...
(laughs)

06:57.110 --> 07:00.144
And then after the funeral,
Angelina Jolie.

07:01.546 --> 07:04.115
I would love to bang Mila Kunis.

07:06.084 --> 07:07.852
Not gonna happen, Barry.

07:08.587 --> 07:10.254
All right. I'm out of here.

07:10.256 --> 07:11.889
I thought we were
gonna grab some dinner.

07:11.891 --> 07:14.025
I can't. I got a thing.

07:14.027 --> 07:15.393
You got a thing. I got a thing.

07:15.395 --> 07:17.528
We put our things together,
we have some fun.

07:18.597 --> 07:19.563
Hey, every time
I say stuff like that,

07:19.565 --> 07:20.931
I get pepper sprayed.

07:20.933 --> 07:24.969
That was one time, Barry and
my mom still feels bad about it.

07:26.304 --> 07:28.639
I'll make it up to you tomorrow,
I promise.

07:29.775 --> 07:31.575
What's your mom up to
these days?

07:31.577 --> 07:33.110
Shut up, Barry.

07:33.112 --> 07:35.012
Better hope I don't
run into Mila Kunis.

07:35.014 --> 07:36.981
(scoffs)
Yeah, like that's gonna happen.

07:38.116 --> 07:40.217
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪
(doorbell rings)

07:42.120 --> 07:43.554
Hey! There's my best man!

07:43.556 --> 07:45.756
Groom goes the dynamite.

07:45.758 --> 07:46.724
(imitates explosion)

07:46.726 --> 07:48.492
(laughing)
Come on in.

07:48.494 --> 07:51.128
I've got some beer on ice
and sports on ice.

07:51.130 --> 07:52.363
Oh, yeah! You're right!

07:52.365 --> 07:54.632
Uh, tonight's the finals
of the pairs ice dancing.

07:54.634 --> 07:56.434
(laughing)

07:56.436 --> 07:57.668
You're hilarious.

07:57.670 --> 07:59.203
Hey, you got to do
this gay character

07:59.205 --> 08:00.604
in your best man toast.

08:00.606 --> 08:03.040
Uh, about that,
you know I'm-I'm-I'm not sure

08:03.042 --> 08:05.643
that I'm the right person
to be your best man.

08:05.645 --> 08:08.112
I'll probably just end up
drinking too much

08:08.114 --> 08:10.247
and getting yelled at
by the bride

08:10.249 --> 08:12.416
and singing a tearful,
yet moving version of

08:12.418 --> 08:13.918
"All by Myself."

08:15.120 --> 08:16.754
At least, that's
what happened at my wedding.

08:16.756 --> 08:18.589
Well, you're not getting
cold feet, are you, buddy?

08:18.591 --> 08:20.558
Well, no, it's just
that it's your special day.

08:20.560 --> 08:22.860
I mean, y-you sure that there
isn't somebody more deserving

08:22.862 --> 08:23.928
to be your best man?

08:23.930 --> 08:26.097
A-a-a brother?
A college roommate?

08:26.099 --> 08:27.731
Someone who knows
your last name?

08:27.733 --> 08:30.101
God, you're a riot.

08:30.103 --> 08:31.268
There's nobody
I'd rather stand with

08:31.270 --> 08:32.570
at that altar than you, Jeff.

08:32.572 --> 08:35.439
(sighs) Why do you have to be
so darn sweet?

08:35.441 --> 08:36.941
Plus, I'm counting on you
to help me out

08:36.943 --> 08:38.442
with the most important part
of this wedding--

08:38.444 --> 08:40.678
bachelor party.
Outfits.

08:41.813 --> 08:43.347
I was thinking black tie.

08:43.349 --> 08:46.016
Sure, black girls, Thai girls,
whatever you want.

08:46.918 --> 08:49.920
Larry, where can I
put this poop?

08:49.922 --> 08:52.723
Ooh!
And who do we have here?

08:53.692 --> 08:55.426
This is my sister Gretchen.
She just moved here.

08:55.428 --> 08:56.994
Gretchen,
this is Jeff Strongman.

08:56.996 --> 08:58.028
Oh, yeah!

08:58.030 --> 08:58.996
Hey, from what I hear,

08:58.998 --> 09:00.297
I should call you
"Jeff Best Man."

09:00.299 --> 09:03.534
(whispering):
Oh, my God, that's what I said.

09:03.536 --> 09:05.169
Um, so, where's your dog?

09:05.171 --> 09:07.304
In the garage
trying to wipe his ass.

09:08.507 --> 09:10.007
Now, I couldn't find the trash.

09:10.009 --> 09:11.976
It's out back.
I got it.

09:11.978 --> 09:13.077
(laughs)
You can tell I love her,

09:13.079 --> 09:14.578
'cause I take
a lot of crap from her.

09:14.580 --> 09:16.814
Get it? Crap.

09:16.816 --> 09:18.182
(laughing)

09:18.184 --> 09:20.050
And he's Mom's favorite.

09:20.052 --> 09:22.586
I hear you.
Luckily, my brother's dead.

09:22.588 --> 09:24.855
Oh.
So...

09:24.857 --> 09:26.690
uh... uh, you just moved here?

09:26.692 --> 09:28.125
Yeah. My brother's
letting me crash here.

09:28.127 --> 09:30.294
I told him it was just
for a couple days,

09:30.296 --> 09:32.830
but, between you and me,
it's a pretty sweet deal.

09:32.832 --> 09:34.498
Huh. I should try that.

09:35.500 --> 09:36.500
Part of me thinks

09:36.502 --> 09:37.868
I should just stay here
till he dies.

09:37.870 --> 09:39.670
Why stop there?

09:39.672 --> 09:41.672
Why not move in with
the next guy who buys the house?

09:41.674 --> 09:42.740
Yeah.

09:42.742 --> 09:43.841
So, uh, what do you do?

09:43.843 --> 09:45.509
I'm a vet.
I moved out here

09:45.511 --> 09:46.511
to run an animal shelter.

09:46.512 --> 09:49.013
Oh... so that
tasteful sports bra

09:49.015 --> 09:50.047
covers a tender heart?

09:50.049 --> 09:52.216
Well, the puppies at the shelter

09:52.218 --> 09:54.385
aren't the only ones
that need support.

09:54.387 --> 09:57.087
Well, I'd uh, I'd love to meet
your furry little friend.

09:57.089 --> 09:58.088
Oh.

09:58.090 --> 09:59.757
I mean, I'm talking
about the dog.

09:59.759 --> 10:00.858
Um...

10:00.860 --> 10:02.493
Not that I don't
want to meet--

10:02.495 --> 10:04.195
Never mind, uh...
(laughs)

10:04.197 --> 10:05.496
So, you run a shelter?

10:05.498 --> 10:07.431
Yeah. I've always had
a soft spot for strays

10:07.433 --> 10:09.066
that no one else wanted
to take in.

10:09.068 --> 10:11.769
(whimpers like a puppy)

10:11.771 --> 10:13.804
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

10:13.806 --> 10:14.598
Hey.

10:14.623 --> 10:16.975
Ho, ho, ho-- somebody
is gettin' laid tonight.

10:16.976 --> 10:18.509
Thank you.

10:18.511 --> 10:19.810
No, not you.

10:19.812 --> 10:22.146
I just found a late night
booty call on Craigslist.

10:22.148 --> 10:24.181
Hello, BoobaFett420.

10:25.083 --> 10:26.250
You know, Barry,

10:26.252 --> 10:28.719
sometimes the picture
isn't who you get.

10:28.721 --> 10:30.087
Oh, tell me about it.

10:30.089 --> 10:31.889
I used your picture.

10:31.891 --> 10:33.557
Where's Nicole?

10:33.559 --> 10:34.558
Ugh. Nicole.

10:34.560 --> 10:36.293
Yikes.

10:36.295 --> 10:37.995
This is gonna be tough.
What happened?

10:37.997 --> 10:40.397
She's dead.
What?

10:40.399 --> 10:41.732
No, she just blew you off again.

10:41.734 --> 10:43.968
I was just trying
to soften the blow.

10:43.970 --> 10:46.503
The second time she canceled.

10:46.505 --> 10:49.206
Something's going on.

10:49.208 --> 10:50.441
Look, I'm sure there is

10:50.443 --> 10:51.875
a perfectly reasonable
explanation.

10:51.877 --> 10:53.177
She say anything?

10:53.179 --> 10:54.612
Just that she would
call you later.

10:54.614 --> 10:56.747
But on the plus side,
I'm available now.

10:56.749 --> 10:59.116
Dave and Buster's, party of two.

10:59.118 --> 11:00.551
We're not going
to Dave and Buster's.

11:00.553 --> 11:02.086
We're gonna track down
my girlfriend.

11:02.088 --> 11:04.088
Now shut up and get in the car.

11:04.090 --> 11:07.358
Oh, my God,
you sound just like my dad.

11:08.059 --> 11:10.394
♪ &lt;i>Men.&lt;/i> ♪

11:10.396 --> 11:12.329
